Actor (Test)
{
	Mesh:Material <Cube>:<DoomMat>
}


#define THEATRE_REFERENCE 0
#define RAW_DATA 1

{{"Actor", {RAW_DATA, "Test"}}, {"Actor:Mesh", {THEATRE_REFERENCE, "Cube"}}, {"Actor:Mesh:Material", {THEATRE_REFERENCE, "DoomMat"}}}

gSettings mesh_settings = {{"Name", "Cube"}, {"Material", new_theatre.getDevice(material_uid)}}

{"Mesh", {devices_map[MESH], mesh_settings}}


variable = new Mesh(mesh_settings)


Mesh::Mesh(gSettings new_settings)
{
	loadSettings(new_settings);
}


The idea is to treat sandwiches the same as theatre references, but I think that it might need to be tweaked.

New Idea: sandwiches are different from theatre references, but are basically just like a nested gSettings with an assigned class type (since sandwiches always result in needing to make a new class anyways). This would also allow for sandwiches to accept any data types.